{"body":"`DeclaredCaps` maintains the inventory of capabilities that built-in agents can expose without advertising them through `DeclaredCapabilities`. That inventory had already drifted more than once: the original documentation missed several helpers, and `ToolInvocationScanner` was added after this PR opened without updating the list.\n\nThis makes the inventory an enforced architectural invariant instead of relying on reviewers to maintain it manually.\n\n## What changed\n\nEvery package-level `As*` capability helper now resolves directly through one of the two standard paths:\n\n- `builtinCapability` for capabilities that do not require declaration\n- `declaredCapability` for capabilities gated by `DeclaredCaps`\n\nThe existing `SidecarImageProvider`, `StreamingTextGenerator`, `ContextInjector`, and `ModelLister` helpers were normalized to that shape without changing their signatures or behavior.\n\nA package-wide AST test now scans production files in the top-level `agent` package and verifies that:\n\n- every `As*` helper uses one of the standard resolvers;\n- the capabilities using `builtinCapability` exactly match the list documented above `DeclaredCaps`;\n- the documented list remains alphabetically sorted.\n\nThis covers helpers outside `capabilities.go`, including `AsContextInjector` and `AsModelLister`, and catches future additions such as `ToolInvocationScanner` automatically.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nThere are no public API or protocol-schema changes. The normalized helpers preserve their existing return values and declaration-gating behavior.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `mise run check`\n- 56/56 Vogon canaries passed\n- 4/4 external-agent canaries passed\n- A controlled mutation removing `ToolInvocationScanner` from the documentation caused the architecture test to fail with the expected inventory mismatch\n","checks":[],"comments":[{"author":"MuskanPaliwal","body":"Hi @Soph , this pr addresses #1877 out-of-scope documentation fix. Would appreciate your review on this. Thanks!"},{"author":"Soph","body":"Verified every entry against the source - an `As*` helper in `capabilities.go` is ungated exactly when it resolves by bare type assertion rather than `declaredCapability[T]`, which is 10 helpers. The list goes from 5/10 to 9/10 with this change, and all four additions are correct. `SessionEndBudgeter` wasn't in the review note you cited, so that one's a genuine find on top of the ask (the PR body "},{"author":"MuskanPaliwal","body":"Thanks @Soph, good catch. I went with the AST-backed option.\n\nThe follow-up commit makes every package-level `As*` helper use either `builtinCapability` or `declaredCapability`. The test scans production files across the top-level `agent` package, so it catches helpers outside `capabilities.go`, including `AsContextInjector` and `AsModelLister`. It derives the built-in set from those helpers and c"},{"author":"MuskanPaliwal","body":"hi @Soph , i have this open for a long, would love to get your feedback here and get it merged . thanks :))"}],"mergeable":"CONFLICTING","reviewDecision":"REVIEW_REQUIRED","reviews":[]}

